\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Summary of convergence and stability diagnostics. \textbf  {E@90\% best}: epoch where the run first attains 90\% of its own best validation score (accuracy or $R^2$). \textbf  {Slope}: change in metric from epoch~1 to~3. Lower E@90\% best and lower stability CVs indicate faster, steadier convergence; higher early slopes indicate faster initial learning.}}{15}{table.caption.31}\protected@file@percent }
